## Finding

**[P2] 313: the numeric-only auto key does not judge the requested method.**
The current prompt explicitly says to calculate using the most reasonable
method. `answer-keys.json:56` sets auto; lines 60-61 only expect 100 and 15.
The display derivations and both results are correct. However, production
`judgeTextbookPart` only parses each numeric submission and checks equivalence;
it cannot see or assess a method. The note at line 63 concedes that loss.
Accepting the two bare results would return a whole-exercise correct verdict
without the method component. The user's explicit review rule forbids treating
equivalence alone as enforcement of a required method.

Narrow correction belongs to parent/author: change 313 to ungraded with
`parts: []`, retain the existing correct display solution, update its note
and the dependent author result/counts. This would leave 14 ungraded exercises
with all 55 concrete display tasks, no machine parts. No prompt change, new
grader, fake method string, new library, or broad rework is required.

